# Python

Target current, typed Python. Use explicit types on public functions and structured return values. Raise specific exceptions; do not swallow them.

Keep I/O, model calls, and pure logic separate so logic can be tested without a network. Prefer the standard library before adding a dependency.

Deterministic code beats a model when the rule is known. Do not hide side effects in constructors or import time.

Configuration comes from the environment or an explicit config object. Never commit secrets, and never log tokens or raw credentials.

Tests assert behavior and edge cases, not private call sequences.
